    },
    {
      "sentence": 180,
      "text": "x.automated contains system test cases for testing the system-automated actions (manually invoked during testing)."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 181,
      "text": "Some Component tests are pure unit tests (i.e. testing one component in isolation) while others are integration tests that test units as well as integration of units with each other."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 182,
      "text": "Front-end files (particularly TypeScript) are tested separately with Jest."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 183,
      "text": "The test cases are found in x.spec.ts files."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 184,
      "text": "This is how TEAMMATES testing maps to standard types of testing."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 185,
      "text": "The E2E component has no knowledge of the internal workings of the application and can only interact either with Web browser as a whole application or REST API calls for the back-end logic."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 186,
      "text": "Its primary function is for E2E tests and L&P (Load & Performance) tests."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 187,
      "text": "Package overview contains e2e.util, e2e.pageobjects, e2e.cases, x.util, x.e2e, x.lnp."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 188,
      "text": "e2e.util contains helpers needed for running E2E tests."
