    {
      "sentence": 62,
      "text": "Second, requests generated by the GAE server are equipped with this privilege."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 63,
      "text": "Third, administrators can manually invoke these requests."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 64,
      "text": "This is particularly useful in testing the actions associated with those requests."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 65,
      "text": "Fourth, request forwarded to the AutomatedServlet."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 66,
      "text": "Fifth, automatedServlet uses the AutomatedActionFactory to generate the matching AutomatedAction object, e.g. CompileLogsAction."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 67,
      "text": "Sixth, automatedServlet executes the action."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 68,
      "text": "Seventh, the corresponding AutomatedAction will be performed, interacting with the Logic component as necessary."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 69,
      "text": "GAE server sends such automated requests through two different configurations."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 70,
      "text": "These configurations are cron jobs or task queue workers."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 71,
      "text": "Cron jobs are jobs that are automatically scheduled for a specified period of time, e.g. scheduling feedback session opening reminders."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 72,
      "text": "It is configured in cron.xml."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 73,
      "text": "Task queue workers are hybrids of user-invoked and GAE-invoked in that they are queued by users (i.e. users request for the tasks to be added to queue), but executed by GAE (i.e. GAE determines when and which tasks in the queue are executed at any point of time)."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 74,
      "text": "This is typically used for tasks that may take a long time to finish and can exceed the 1 minute standard request processing limit imposed by GAE."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 75,
      "text": "It is configured in queue.xml as well as the TaskQueue nested class of the Const class."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 76,
      "text": "Since the high-level workflow of processing a request is same for any request (differing by the two request types only), we use the Template Method pattern to abstract the process flow into the Action and AutomatedAction classes."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 77,
      "text": "The Logic component handles the business logic of TEAMMATES."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 78,
      "text": "In particular, it is responsible for the following."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 79,
      "text": "Managing relationships between entities, e.g. cascade logic for create/update/delete."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 80,
      "text": "Managing transactions, e.g. ensuring atomicity of a transaction."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 81,
      "text": "Sanitizing input values received from the UI component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 82,
      "text": "Providing a mechanism for checking access control rights."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 83,
      "text": "Connecting to GAE-provided or third-party APIs, e.g. for adding tasks to the task queue and for sending emails with third-party providers."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 84,
      "text": "Package overview contains logic.api, logic.core."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 85,
      "text": "logic.api provides the API of the component to be accessed by the UI."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 86,
      "text": "logic.core contains the core logic of the system."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 87,
      "text": "Logic API is represented by the classes Logic, GateKeeper, EmailGenerator, EmailSender, TaskQueuer."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 88,
      "text": "Logic is a Facade class which connects to the several Logic classes to handle the logic related to various types of data and to access data from the Storage component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 89,
      "text": "GateKeeper checks access rights of a user for a given action."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 90,
      "text": "EmailGenerator generates emails to be sent."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 91,
      "text": "EmailSender sends email with the provider chosen based on the build configuration."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 92,
      "text": "It connects to the email provider by using the appropriate Service class."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 93,
      "text": "TaskQueuer adds tasks to the task queue."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 94,
      "text": "It connects to GAE's task queue API."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 95,
      "text": "To access control the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 96,
      "text": "Although this component provides methods to perform access control, the API itself is not access controlled."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 97,
      "text": "The UI is expected to check access control (using GateKeeper class) before calling a method in the Logic."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 98,
      "text": "To API for creating entities the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 99,
      "text": "Null parameters causes an assertion failure."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 100,
      "text": "Invalid parameters throws InvalidParametersException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 101,
      "text": "Entity already exists throws EntityAlreadyExistsException (escalated from Storage level)."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 102,
      "text": "To API for retrieving entities the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 103,
      "text": "Attempting to retrieve objects using null parameters causes an assertion failure."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 104,
      "text": "Entity not found returns null if the target entity not found."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 105,
      "text": "This way, read operations can be used easily for checking the existence of an entity."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 106,
      "text": "To API for updating entities the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 107,
      "text": "Update is done using UpdateOptions inside every Attributes."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 108,
      "text": "The UpdateOptions will specify what is used to identify the entity to update and what will be updated."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 109,
      "text": "Entity not found throws EntityDoesNotExistException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 110,
      "text": "Invalid parameters throws InvalidParametersException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 111,
      "text": "To API for deleting entities the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 112,
      "text": "The following explains the FailDeleteSilentlyPolicy."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 113,
      "text": "In general, delete operation do not throw exceptions if the target entity does not exist."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 114,
      "text": "This is because if it does not exist, it is as good as deleted."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 115,
      "text": "The following explains the Cascade policy."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 116,
      "text": "When a parent entity is deleted, entities that have referential integrity with the deleted entity should also be deleted."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 117,
      "text": "Refer to the API for the cascade logic."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 118,
      "text": "The Storage component performs CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations on data entities individually."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 119,
      "text": "It contains minimal logic beyond what is directly relevant to CRUD operations."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 120,
      "text": "In particular, it is reponsible for the following."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 121,
      "text": "Validating data inside entities before creating/updating them, to ensure they are in a valid state."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 122,
      "text": "Hiding the complexities of datastore from the Logic component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 123,
      "text": "All GQL queries are to be contained inside the Storage component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 124,
      "text": "Hiding the persistable objects."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 125,
      "text": "Classes in the storage.entity package are not visible outside this component to hide information specific to data persistence."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 126,
      "text": "Instead, a corresponding non-persistent data transfer object named Attributes (e.g., CourseAttributes is the data transfer object for Course entities) object is returned."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 127,
      "text": "These datatransfer classes are in common.datatransfer package, to be explained later."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 128,
      "text": "The Storage component does not perform any cascade delete/create operations."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 129,
      "text": "Cascade logic is handled by the Logic component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 130,
      "text": "Package overview contains storage.api, storage.entity, storage.search."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 131,
      "text": "storage.api provides the API of the component to be accessed by the logic component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 132,
      "text": "storage.entity contains classes that represent persistable entities."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 133,
      "text": "storage.search contains classes for dealing with searching and indexing."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 134,
      "text": "Note that the navigability of the association links between entity objects appear to be in the reverse direction of what we see in a normal OOP design."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 135,
      "text": "This is because we want to keep the data schema flexible so that new entity types can be added later with minimal modifications to existing elements."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 136,
      "text": "Represented by the Db classes."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 137,
      "text": "These classes act as the bridge to the GAE Datastore."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 138,
      "text": "Add and Delete operations try to wait until data is persisted in the datastore before returning."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 139,
      "text": "This is not enough to compensate for eventual consistency involving multiple servers in the GAE production environment."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 140,
      "text": "However, it is expected to avoid test failures caused by eventual consistency in dev server and reduce such problems in the live server."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 141,
      "text": "Eventual consistency here means it takes some time for a database operation to propagate across all serves of the Google's distributed datastore."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 142,
      "text": "As a result, the data may be in an inconsistent states for short periods of time although things should become consistent eventually."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 143,
      "text": "For example, an object we deleted may appear to still exist for a short while."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 144,
      "text": "Implementation of Transaction Control has been minimized due to limitations of GAE environment and the nature of our data schema."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 145,
      "text": "To API for creating the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 146,
      "text": "Attempt to create an entity that already exists throws EntityAlreadyExistsException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 147,
      "text": "Attempt to create an entity with invalid data throws InvalidParametersException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 148,
      "text": "To API for retrieving the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 149,
      "text": "Attempt to retrieve an entity that does not exist returns null."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 150,
      "text": "To API for updating the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 151,
      "text": "Attempt to update an entity that does not exist throws EntityDoesNotExistException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 152,
      "text": "Attempt to update an entity with invalid data throws InvalidParametersException."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 153,
      "text": "To API for deleting the following information are presented."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 154,
      "text": "Attempt to delete an entity that does not exist fails silently."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 155,
      "text": "The Common component contains common utilities used across TEAMMATES."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 156,
      "text": "Package overview contains common.util, common.exceptions, common.datatransfer."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 157,
      "text": "common.util contains utility classes."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 158,
      "text": "common.exceptions contains custom exceptions."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 159,
      "text": "common.datatransfer contains data transfer objects."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 160,
      "text": "common.datatransfer package contains lightweight data transfer object classes for transferring data among components."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 161,
      "text": "They can be combined in various ways to transfer structured data between components."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 162,
      "text": "Given below are three examples."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 163,
      "text": "Test Driver can use the DataBundle in this manner to send an arbitrary number of objects to be persisted in the database."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 164,
      "text": "This structure can be used to transfer data of a course (e.g., when constructing the home page for an instructor)."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 165,
      "text": "This structure can be used to send results of a feedback session (e.g., when showing a feedback session report to an instructor)."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 166,
      "text": "Some of these classes are methodless and thus more of a data structure rather than a class."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 167,
      "text": "These classes use public variables for data for easy access."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 168,
      "text": "This component automates the testing of TEAMMATES."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 169,
      "text": "Package overview contains test.driver, test.cases and subpackages."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 170,
      "text": "test.driver contains infrastructure and helpers needed for running the tests."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 171,
      "text": "test.cases contains test cases."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 172,
      "text": "Sub-packages contains x.testdriver, x.datatransfer, x.util, x.logic, x.storage, x.search, x.webapi, x.automated."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 173,
      "text": "x.testdriver contains component test cases for testing the test driver infrastructure and helpers."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 174,
      "text": "x.datatransfer contains component test cases for testing the datatransfer objects from the Common component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 175,
      "text": "x.util contains component test cases for testing the utility classes from the Common component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 176,
      "text": "x.logic contains component test cases for testing the Logic component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 177,
      "text": "x.storage contains component test cases for testing the Storage component."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 178,
      "text": "x.search contains component test cases for testing the search functions."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 179,
      "text": "x.webapi contains system test cases for testing the user-invoked actions."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 180,
      "text": "x.automated contains system test cases for testing the system-automated actions (manually invoked during testing)."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 181,
      "text": "Some Component tests are pure unit tests (i.e. testing one component in isolation) while others are integration tests that test units as well as integration of units with each other."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 182,
      "text": "Front-end files (particularly TypeScript) are tested separately with Jest."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 183,
      "text": "The test cases are found in x.spec.ts files."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 184,
      "text": "This is how TEAMMATES testing maps to standard types of testing."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 185,
      "text": "The E2E component has no knowledge of the internal workings of the application and can only interact either with Web browser as a whole application or REST API calls for the back-end logic."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 186,
      "text": "Its primary function is for E2E tests and L&P (Load & Performance) tests."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 187,
      "text": "Package overview contains e2e.util, e2e.pageobjects, e2e.cases, x.util, x.e2e, x.lnp."
    },
    {
      "sentence": 188,
      "text": "e2e.util contains helpers needed for running E2E tests."
    },
